    That is not the whole of the BayesTS core, only what the four dynamic
    factor models and the factor augmented VAR reach -- this package has
    those five samplers and does not need the other fifteen. tools/update-bayests-core.R computes that
    set by following the #include graph from them, so the list above is
    derived rather than curated, and the script refuses to finish when the
    two disagree.

    inst/include/bayests_reporter.h is *not* part of this set. It lives one
    directory up, belongs to this package rather than to BayesTS, and is
    GPL (>= 2) like the rest of the package. So is
    src/bayests_rng_guard.cpp, which only asserts something about the
    vendored headers, and src/DfmNormalGamma.cpp,
    src/DfmNormalStochvol.cpp, src/DfmTvpGamma.cpp and
    src/DfmTvpStochvol.cpp, which are the translation between an R model
    object and the core's structs.

Code previously published in bvartools
--------------------------------------

    create_dfmodel(), add_priors.dfmodel(), add_initial_values.dfmodel()
    and the bem_dfmdata data set were released in bvartools
    (https://github.com/franzmohr/bvartools) before they moved here. Those
    releases were made under GPL (>= 2) and remain available under those
    terms; this package carries the same license so that the same code does
    not go out under two different notices.

The bem_dfmdata data set
------------------------

    Not this package's data. It is derived from FRED-QD, redistributed via
    the data sets that accompany

        Chan, J., Koop, G., Poirier, D. J., & Tobias, J. L. (2019).
        Bayesian econometric methods (2nd ed.). Cambridge University Press.

    and documented in

        McCracken, M. W., & Ng, S. (2016). FRED-MD: A monthly database for
        macroeconomic research. Journal of Business & Economic Statistics,
        34(4), 574-589.

    The package license is a grant over this package's own work and does not
    purport to license the underlying series, whose terms are the Federal
    Reserve Bank of St. Louis's and the original sources'. data-raw/ records
    how the object was produced from them. Anyone redistributing this data
    set onward, or using it commercially, should check those terms rather
    than rely on the notice at the top of this file.

